---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { getLangFromUrl } from "../../../i18n/utils";

export async function getStaticPaths() {
    return [{ params: { locale: "en" } }, { params: { locale: "it" } }];
}

const locale = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);

const content = {
    en: {
        title: "Mobile backend modernization",
        subtitle: "Kotlin + Spring Boot rewrite using hexagonal architecture",
        period: "Oct - Dec 2024",
        overview:
            "I rewrote the backend for a long-lived KMP mobile app, moving from Java + MyBatis to Kotlin + Spring Boot. The goal was practical: make the code easier to change, safer to run, and faster to reason about. The rewrite reduced boilerplate and improved day-to-day developer ergonomics.",
        challenge:
            "The old backend carried a decade of patches: business logic mixed in MyBatis mappers, different database dialects, and fragile upgrade paths. Small changes could ripple across systems. Shipping reliable fixes took too long.",
        solution:
            "I rewrote the service in Kotlin with Spring Boot and Kotlin Exposed. I focused on small, testable modules and a hexagonal structure so the core logic lives alone and adapters do the dirty work. That made tests simpler, database changes safer, and future refactors less scary.",
        keyAchievements: [
            {
                title: "Cleaner language",
                description:
                    "Moved the codebase to Kotlin. Less boilerplate, clearer null handling, and more expressive APIs made daily work noticeably faster.",
            },
            {
                title: "Safer database access",
                description:
                    "Replaced MyBatis with Kotlin Exposed to get compile-time type checks for queries and fewer runtime surprises.",
            },
            {
                title: "Hexagonal architecture",
                description:
                    "Separated business rules from I/O (API, DB). That paid off immediately: I could run unit tests without spinning up databases.",
            },
            {
                title: "Multi-database compatibility",
                description:
                    "Kept compatibility with MySQL, Oracle and SQL Server while moving the code to a single, consistent data-access layer.",
            },
            {
                title: "Practical quality gains",
                description:
                    "Introduced consistent error handling, better logging, and test containers for integration tests — real things that make debugging less painful.",
            },
        ],
        technologies: [
            { name: "Kotlin", proficiency: "Expert" },
            { name: "Spring Boot", proficiency: "Expert" },
            { name: "Kotlin Exposed", proficiency: "Advanced" },
            { name: "PostgreSQL", proficiency: "Advanced" },
            { name: "Oracle DB", proficiency: "Intermediate" },
            { name: "SQL Server", proficiency: "Intermediate" },
        ],
        techStack: {
            title: "Technical stack",
            items: [
                {
                    category: "Backend",
                    items: ["Kotlin", "Spring Boot", "Coroutines"],
                },
                { category: "ORM", items: ["Kotlin Exposed", "Spring Data"] },
                {
                    category: "Databases",
                    items: ["PostgreSQL", "MySQL", "Oracle", "SQL Server"],
                },
                {
                    category: "API",
                    items: ["REST", "Serialization", "Validation"],
                },
                {
                    category: "Testing",
                    items: ["JUnit 5", "Testcontainers", "MockK"],
                },
                { category: "DevOps", items: ["Docker", "Flyway"] },
            ],
        },
        metrics: [
            { label: "Less boilerplate", value: "≈40%" },
            { label: "Test coverage", value: "85%+" },
            { label: "Databases supported", value: "3" },
            { label: "Perf improvement", value: "+15%" },
        ],
        learnings: [
            "Small, opinionated conventions beat vague patterns when multiple DBs are involved.",
            "Hexagonal boundaries make refactors low-risk. I wish I'd done this sooner.",
            "Type-safe queries save time during debugging — the IDE becomes your friend.",
            "Backward compatibility matters: we kept the old DBs while moving forward.",
        ],
    },
    it: {
        title: "Modernizzazione backend mobile",
        subtitle:
            "Riscrittura in Kotlin + Spring Boot con architettura esagonale",
        period: "Ott - Dic 2024",
        overview:
            "Ho riscritto il backend di un'app mobile KMP, passando da Java + MyBatis a Kotlin + Spring Boot. L'obiettivo era concreto: semplificare le modifiche, ridurre i bug a runtime e rendere il codice più leggibile. La riscrittura ha ridotto il boilerplate e reso il lavoro quotidiano più fluido.",
        challenge:
            "Il vecchio backend portava con sé anni di patch: logica di business sparsa tra mapper MyBatis, dialetti diversi per database e upgrade delicati. Anche piccole modifiche potevano avere effetti a catena. Risolvere bug era lento e rischioso.",
        solution:
            "Ho scelto Kotlin e Spring Boot con Kotlin Exposed. Ho strutturato il codice in moduli testabili e ho applicato l'architettura esagonale: la logica sta al centro, gli adapter gestiscono I/O. I test unitari sono diventati più semplici e le modifiche al DB più sicure.",
        keyAchievements: [
            {
                title: "Codice più pulito",
                description:
                    "La migrazione a Kotlin ha ridotto il boilerplate, migliorato il trattamento dei null e reso le API più espressive — si lavora molto meglio.",
            },
            {
                title: "Accesso DB più sicuro",
                description:
                    "Ho sostituito MyBatis con Kotlin Exposed per avere controlli a compile-time sulle query e meno sorprese a runtime.",
            },
            {
                title: "Architettura esagonale",
                description:
                    "Separando regole di business e I/O, ho potuto eseguire test senza avviare database pesanti.",
            },
            {
                title: "Compatibilità multi-database",
                description:
                    "Abbiamo mantenuto il supporto per MySQL, Oracle e SQL Server usando un unico layer di accesso ai dati.",
            },
            {
                title: "Qualità pratica",
                description:
                    "Ho introdotto gestione errori coerente, logging migliore e test d'integrazione con Testcontainers — cose che semplificano il debugging.",
            },
        ],
        technologies: [
            { name: "Kotlin", proficiency: "Esperto" },
            { name: "Spring Boot", proficiency: "Esperto" },
            { name: "Kotlin Exposed", proficiency: "Avanzato" },
            { name: "PostgreSQL", proficiency: "Avanzato" },
            { name: "Oracle DB", proficiency: "Intermedio" },
            { name: "SQL Server", proficiency: "Intermedio" },
        ],
        techStack: {
            title: "Stack tecnologico",
            items: [
                {
                    category: "Backend",
                    items: ["Kotlin", "Spring Boot", "Coroutines"],
                },
                { category: "ORM", items: ["Kotlin Exposed", "Spring Data"] },
                {
                    category: "Database",
                    items: ["PostgreSQL", "MySQL", "Oracle", "SQL Server"],
                },
                {
                    category: "API",
                    items: ["REST", "Serialization", "Validation"],
                },
                {
                    category: "Testing",
                    items: ["JUnit 5", "Testcontainers", "MockK"],
                },
                { category: "DevOps", items: ["Docker", "Flyway"] },
            ],
        },
        metrics: [
            { label: "Meno boilerplate", value: "≈40%" },
            { label: "Coverage test", value: "85%+" },
            { label: "DB supportati", value: "3" },
            { label: "Miglioramento perf.", value: "+15%" },
        ],
        learnings: [
            "Convenzioni semplici e opinative aiutano quando ci sono più database.",
            "Confini chiari tra dominio e adapter riducono i rischi durante i refactor.",
            "Le query type-safe fanno risparmiare tempo: l'IDE rileva molti errori prima che vengano eseguiti.",
            "Mantenere compatibilità con i sistemi legacy è spesso più importante di una riscrittura radicale.",
        ],
    },
};

const page = content[locale];
---

<BaseLayout>
    <div
        class="min-h-screen bg-primary dark:bg-secondary text-secondary dark:text-primary"
    >
        <!-- Hero -->
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-20">
            <div class="mb-4">
                <span
                    class="text-sm font-medium text-secondary/60 dark:text-primary/60"
                    >{page.period}</span
                >
            </div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">{page.title}</h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-secondary/80 dark:text-primary/80 mb-8">
                {page.subtitle}
            </p>
            <p
                class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75"
            >
                {page.overview}
            </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Challenge & Solution -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        {locale === "it" ? "Sfida" : "Challenge"}
                    </h2>
                    <p
                        class="text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75 leading-relaxed"
                    >
                        {page.challenge}
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">
                        {locale === "it" ? "Soluzione" : "Solution"}
                    </h2>
                    <p
                        class="text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75 leading-relaxed"
                    >
                        {page.solution}
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Achievements -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">
                {locale === "it" ? "Risultati" : "Key achievements"}
            </h2>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
                {
                    page.keyAchievements.map((a) => (
                        <div class="border-l-2 border-secondary/30 dark:border-primary/30 pl-6 py-2">
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">
                                {a.title}
                            </h3>
                            <p class="text-secondary/70 dark:text-primary/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                                {a.description}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Metrics -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">
                {locale === "it" ? "Impatto" : "Impact"}
            </h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-6">
                {
                    page.metrics.map((m) => (
                        <div class="text-center">
                            <p class="text-4xl font-bold text-secondary dark:text-primary mb-2">
                                {m.value}
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-secondary/60 dark:text-primary/60">
                                {m.label}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Tech Stack -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">{page.techStack.title}</h2>
            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
                {
                    page.techStack.items.map((section) => (
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="font-semibold text-lg mb-3 text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                {section.category}
                            </h3>
                            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                                {section.items.map((item) => (
                                    <span class="px-3 py-1 text-sm bg-secondary/10 dark:bg-primary/10 rounded-full text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                        {item}
                                    </span>
                                ))}
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Technologies -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-8">
                {locale === "it" ? "Tecnologie" : "Technologies used"}
            </h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                {
                    page.technologies.map((tech) => (
                        <div class="p-4 border border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20 rounded-lg">
                            <p class="font-medium text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                {tech.name}
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-secondary/60 dark:text-primary/60">
                                {tech.proficiency}
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    ))
                }
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Learnings -->
        <div
            class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16 border-t border-secondary/20 dark:border-primary/20 mb-20"
        >
            <h2 class="text-3xl font-semibold mb-4">
                {locale === "it" ? "Lezioni imparate" : "Key learnings"}
            </h2>
            <ul class="space-y-3 text-secondary/75 dark:text-primary/75">
                {
                    page.learnings.map((l) => (
                        <li class="flex gap-3">
                            <span class="text-secondary dark:text-primary">
                                ▸
                            </span>
                            <span>{l}</span>
                        </li>
                    ))
                }
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>
